# HotBiteEngine - Visual Studio / MSBuild / CMake build output.
#
# This file was rewritten from a ~900-line dump of individually-listed
# untracked paths (evidently pasted in from repeated `git status` output over
# time) into proper patterns. See git history if any of those literal entries
# are ever needed again.

# Any dotfile/dot-directory anywhere (.vs/, .vscode/, .idea/, etc.) - nothing
# under a leading-dot path in this repo is meant to be tracked.
.*

#--- Build output directories (every project's Debug/Release/x64/x86) --------
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
Release_Production/
x64/
x86/
ipch/

#--- Build/link artifacts (any project, any configuration) -------------------
*.obj
*.exe
*.dll
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.cso
*.res
*.resources
*.aps

#--- MSBuild incremental-build bookkeeping ------------------------------------
*.tlog
*.log
*.lastbuildstate
*.recipe
*.metagen
*.cache
*.CopyComplete
*.FileListAbsolute.txt
*.Up2Date
*.obj.dt.*.json*

#--- Visual Studio user/IDE state (never shared) ------------------------------
*.user
*.suo
*.sdf
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.VC.db-shm
*.VC.db-wal
*.vsidx
*.ncb

#--- CMake (enet, React3d's helloworld/test/testbed sub-builds) --------------
out/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
*.ninja
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log

#--- NuGet package restore (Solution/packages/*, restored by MSBuild) --------
Solution/packages/

#--- Runtime output the tools themselves write, not source ------------------
# Crash reports (see CLAUDE.md's automation "Crashes and hangs" section) and
# the editor's per-run ImGui layout/log, all written by SceneEditor.exe/
# Marbles.exe at run time, never authored.
crash.dmp
crash.txt
imgui.ini
scene_editor_log.txt

#--- Large/regenerable test assets deliberately kept out of the repo --------
Tests/DemoGame/assets/particle_test.blend1
Tests/DemoGame/assets/Objects/oct.ply
Tests/DemoGame/assets/Objects/scene.ply
Tests/DemoGame/assets/splats/oct.ply

# LOD mesh cache: keyed by vertex/index counts, not content, and rebuilt
# automatically from the "generated_meshes" recipe already saved in each
# level.json the first time that level loads (see World::Load).
GeneratedMeshes/
